      "known_approximation": "The mass channel mirrors the repo's GENERIC term config gear_sonic/config/manager_env/events/terms/randomize_rigid_body_mass.yaml (scale [0.8,1.2] over body_names '.*'), NOT the campaign's RESOLVED event, which was scale [0.8,1.5] over body_names '.*wrist_yaw.*|torso_link' (config.yaml:872-884 of sonic_release_test-20260830_002425). Friction is likewise a single geom_friction scalar clipped to [0.05,4.0], where Isaac draws static [0.3,1.6], dynamic [0.3,1.2] and restitution [0.0,0.5] into 64 buckets. This is why the replay is described as a labelled approximation and the absolute gap is reported, not tuned."
    },
    "survival_definition": {
      "operational": "At every 20 ms control step the 3-D distance between the pelvis body position and the reference root position is computed; if it ever exceeds 0.5 m the run FAILS and t_end is the fall time. A run PASSES only if the distance stays under 0.5 m for the whole 4.0 s clip (mujoco_player.py:566-573).",
      "threshold_provenance": "0.5 m is the anchor_pos termination threshold used in every Isaac scored cell",
      "not": "This is a survival/anchoring criterion, not a tracking-quality criterion. It says nothing about MPJPE."
    },
