      "channel_set_caveat": "Neither MuJoCo sweep matches the Isaac ladder's channel set exactly. Isaac's phys_* ladder scales five channels INCLUDING push and pins latency to zero. MuJoCo 'all channels' adds a delay channel on top of those five; MuJoCo 'physics only' drops push and keeps delay."
    },
    "where_the_ordering_does_and_does_not_hold": {
      "holds_beyond_the_envelope": "At lambda 1.5 and 2.0 the collapsed policy sits below never-shrink and both fixed arms in both sweeps, and no-DR is last everywhere at lambda >= 1.",
      "fails_inside_the_envelope": "At lambda 1 the COLLAPSED policy outranks never-shrink and paired fixed in BOTH sweeps (physics-only 27/32 = 84.4% vs ratchet 21/32 = 65.6% and fixed_s8601 24/32 = 75.0%; all-channels 18/32 = 56.2% vs 15/32 = 46.9% for both). At lambda 1.25 (all channels) the three tie at 10/32. Isaac-vs-MuJoCo rank correlation at lambda 1 is only 0.40 (physics-only) / 0.56 (all channels), versus 0.90 and 0.97 beyond the envelope.",
      "consequence_for_the_paper": "The transferable claim is 'the ordering transfers BEYOND the training envelope', not 'the ordering transfers'. The README's sentence 'the ordering ... holds from lambda 1 up' is contradicted by the data."
    },
    "sim2sim_gap": {
      "statement": "Absolute MuJoCo survival is far below the Isaac ledger for the same checkpoints and the same nominal lambda; e.g. at lambda 2 physics-only ratchet_s8601 is 37.5% in MuJoCo against 83.2% in Isaac, and fixed_s8600 is 31.2% against 82.0%. The gap is reported, not tuned.",
      "cause": "different randomization implementation (see known_approximation) plus a different physics engine and contact model"
    },
